            <ArticleTitle>A proposed model for improving battlefield analgesia training: post-graduate medical officer pain management day.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In response to increasing awareness of the need to improve Post Graduate Medical Officers training in the use of analgesics when on Operations and exercises, a new &quot;Pain Day&quot; format has been realised and included in the Post Graduate Medical Officers Course. This article discusses the format of the Pain Day; gives evidence of the feedback received; explores areas where further training may be required and suggests mechanisms through which improved training could be provided throughout the armed forces medical community.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
